  - compute_mixed_s_matrix: the N-probe |Zc| fit for MSL port 'msl_0' deviates up to 26.8% from analytic Hammerstad-Jensen 47.89 ohm. The MSL diagonal here uses the ANALYTIC anchor, so this does not change the returned S — it is a diagnostic that the record may be under-settled (check settling_db) or the discretized line genuinely differs (Yee staircase on coarse meshes).
  - standing-wave null at the port plane: 2 bins in [3.2500, 4.0000] GHz have |V|,|I| below 10% of band median — wave-split S-parameters are unreliable there (blind spot of single-run reflection measurements of strong reflectors); see rfx-known-issues standing-wave-null entry
  - S-matrix projected onto the passive set (singular values clipped to 1): 5 of 5 frequency bins were non-passive as extracted, worst sigma_max = 1.187 at 4.000 GHz. 5 bins exceeded the 1.05 extraction envelope — at those bins the RAW value is a measurement artifact (see reliable / settling_db for the cause) and the projected value inherits that uncertainty; do not quote them as physics. Raw values are preserved in S_raw; corrections per bin in passivity_correction.
  - compute_mixed_s_matrix: reciprocity deviation max 10.5% between |S[0,1]| and |S[1,0]| (tolerance 6%). For a reciprocal structure these must agree; a disagreement means one DRIVEN-port diagonal is wrong (the diagonals set the incident-power normalization P_inc = P_net/(1-|S_jj|^2)), or a flux surface is mis-signed. Note the per-column power sum CANNOT detect this — it is an identity on this channel. Inspect the diagonals and settling_db before quoting any |S|.

